---
title: Healthy chicken katsu curry
servings: 2
course: dinner
cuisine: Japanese
tags: dinner, main course, supper
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/chicken-katsu-curry
time: 55m
---

Heat the #oven{} to 220C/200C fan/gas 7, or if using an #air-fryer{}, heat to 180C for ~{4%minutes}. Cook the @long-grain brown rice{100%g} in plenty of boiling water for ~{35%minutes} or until tender.

Crush the @flaked almond{25%g} using a #pestle and mortar{} or blitz in a #food processor{} until finely chopped, then sprinkle over a #plate{}. Grease a small #baking tray{} with a little of the @cold-pressed rapeseed oil{1%tsp} if baking in the #oven{}. Brush the @chicken breast{2} on both sides with the remaining @&cold-pressed rapeseed oil{} and season well. Coat the chicken with the nuts and place on the tray. Press any remaining nuts from the plate onto each breast. Bake for ~{20%minutes} in the oven, or ~{18-20%minutes} in the air-fryer until browned and cooked through. Rest for ~{4-5%minutes} on the tray, then slice thickly.

Meanwhile, make the sauce. Heat the @&cold-pressed rapeseed oil{2%tsp} in a medium non-stick #saucepan{} and add the @onion{1} roughly chopped, @garlic clove{2} finely chopped and @ginger{1%piece} peeled and finely chopped. Loosely cover the pan and fry gently for ~{8%minutes} or until softened and lightly browned, stirring occasionally. Remove the lid for the final ~{2%minutes}, and don’t let the garlic burn.

Stir in the @medium curry powder{2%tsp}, @star anise{1}, @ground turmeric{0.25%tsp} and a good grinding of @-black pepper{}. Cook for a few secs more, stirring. Sprinkle over the @plain wholemeal flour{1%tbsp} and stir well. Gradually add @water{400%ml} to the pan, stirring constantly.

Bring the sauce to a simmer and cook for ~{10%minutes}, stirring occasionally. If it begins to splutter, cover loosely with a lid. Remove the pan from the heat and blitz the sauce with a #stick blender{} until smooth. Adjust the seasoning to taste. Keep warm.

Once the rice is tender, add the @spring onion{2} finely sliced and cook for ~{1%minute} more. Drain well, then leave to stand for a few mins while you make the salad. Toss the @carrot{1} peeled into long strips with a vegetable peeler and @cucumber{0.33} peeled into long strips with a vegetable peeler with the @red chilli{1} finely chopped, @lime juice{0.5%lime} and @mint leaf{1%handful} and @coriander leaf{1%handful}.

Divide the sliced chicken between two plates, pour over the sauce and serve with the rice, salad and @lime wedge{1} for squeezing over.
